meta {
  name: GET orderCount()
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/orderCount()
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
}

docs {
  ## Calling the function

  Straight off the service root — no entity set, no key. The empty
  parentheses mark it as a function call, not a property.

  Expected: 200 OK with { "value": N } — OData wraps a scalar return in
  "value". N is the number of orders so far (1 seed + each duplicate).
  Send it again: same answer, nothing changes.
}
